asr-000033
00:28:45.800 --> 00:29:02.940
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management, we have Director Elena Regina Brillantes, Ms. Siti Nor Ayma Dimapanat, Ms. Patricia Arabella Villamin, Ms. Christine Love Morales, Ms. Najla Marie Kawaling, and Mr. Clarence Ivar Odsinada. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000034
00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:18.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, our Committee Secretary. At this juncture, the Chair would like to give his opening statement. Today, we take up the proposed 2027 budget of the Commission Audit, our Constitutional Guardian of Public Funds.

asr-000035
00:29:18.020 --> 00:29:32.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At a time when public confidence in government spending is being tested, COA must be equipped to detect wrongdoing early, verify that projects exist, and work as intended.

asr-000036
00:29:32.940 --> 00:29:46.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And hold accountable those who misuse public money. We also want to recognize the men and women of COA who carry out this difficult mandate every day. Their work is often difficult, technical, and done away from public attention.

asr-000037
00:29:47.400 --> 00:30:00.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Audit observations and notices of disallowance are not always well received, but are part of the checks and balances that protect public funds. Government agencies should see them not as an attack, but as

asr-000038
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:05.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: an opportunity to explain, correct deficiencies, strengthen internal controls, and improve

asr-000039
00:30:05.920 --> 00:30:07.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the use of public funds.

asr-000040
00:30:07.840 --> 00:30:13.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We want to know whether the funding level under 2027 NEP is enough for the job we expect

asr-000041
00:30:13.080 --> 00:30:14.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: COA to perform.

asr-000042
00:30:14.860 --> 00:30:20.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We will look closely at your capacity for fraud and performance audits, field inspections,

asr-000043
00:30:21.120 --> 00:30:28.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: information system audits, citizen participation, staffing, and the timely resolution of audit

asr-000044
00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:28.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: findings.

asr-000045
00:30:28.660 --> 00:30:31.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At the same time, accountability must begin at home.

asr-000046
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:36.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: COA itself must meet the same standards of sound financial management, transparency,

asr-000047
00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:40.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and internal control that it requires from every government agency.

asr-000048
00:30:40.860 --> 00:30:42.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our objective is simple.

asr-000049
00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:48.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Every peso we provide to COA should help protect many more pesos from waste, irregularity,

asr-000050
00:30:48.380 --> 00:30:49.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and corruption.

asr-000051
00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:56.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At this point, since our colleagues are not yet here, we'll just ask them for their

asr-000052
00:30:56.360 --> 00:30:58.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: manifestations and their queries later.

asr-000053
00:30:58.660 --> 00:31:06.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, may we request the Commission on Audit to brief us on the proposed fiscal year 2027

asr-000054
00:31:06.720 --> 00:31:08.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: National Expenditure Program.

asr-000055
00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:14.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I ask the indulgence of the others to allow the Commission to present and complete their

asr-000056
00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:14.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: presentation.

asr-000057
00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:19.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Chairman Gamaliel Cordoba, you now have the floor.

asr-000058
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:25.000
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Opo. Good afternoon to the Honorable Chairperson of the Committee on Finance, Senator JV

asr-000059
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:28.400
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Ejercito, and to the personnel and officials of

asr-000060
00:31:28.660 --> 00:31:31.160
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: the Committee on Finance of the Senate.

asr-000061
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:35.920
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Good afternoon, everyone, and thank you very much for having us this afternoon.

asr-000062
00:31:36.840 --> 00:31:44.760
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: May I ask Nilda Plaras to present the details of our budget.

asr-000063
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:45.680
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Thank you very much.

asr-000064
00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:51.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Assistant Commissioner Nilda Plaras, you now have the floor for the presentation.

asr-000065
00:31:52.220 --> 00:31:56.480
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Good afternoon, Chairperson of the Committee on Finance.

asr-000066
00:31:56.480 --> 00:31:57.620
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Good afternoon, everyone.

asr-000067
00:31:57.620 --> 00:32:00.520
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: My fellow COAns and public servants.

asr-000068
00:32:02.140 --> 00:32:09.500
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: At this point, I will present to you the major accomplishments of the Commission on Audit

asr-000069
00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:19.340
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: for fiscal year 2025 and first semester of fiscal year 2026, as well as the budget of

asr-000070
00:32:19.340 --> 00:32:23.220
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: the Commission on Audit for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000071
00:32:23.740 --> 00:32:28.250
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Under the financial performance.

asr-000072
00:32:28.430 --> 00:32:55.120
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As of December 31, 2025, the Commission on Audit received a total allotment of $15.1 billion, and out of this total allotment, 97.36%, or $14.7 billion, was obligated.

asr-000073
00:32:55.120 --> 00:33:21.740
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And out of this total obligations incurred of $14.7 billion, 97.33%, or $14.3 billion, was disbursed, resulting to the balances of unobligated allotment of $398 million, and unpaid obligations of $392 million.

asr-000074
00:33:21.740 --> 00:33:47.950
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For the first semester of fiscal year 2026, COA has an allotment, a total allotment of $15.7 billion, and out of this $15.7 billion, 51.06%, or $8 billion, was obligated.

asr-000075
00:33:47.950 --> 00:33:52.950
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And out of this total obligations incurred, 97.3%.

asr-000076
00:33:52.990 --> 00:33:58.610
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And out of this total obligations incurred, 97.45%, or $7.8 billion, was disbursed.

asr-000077
00:33:59.210 --> 00:34:06.830
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Excuse me, Assistant Commissioner. Our Blue Ribbon Chair, Senator Erwin Tulfo, has joined us.

asr-000078
00:34:06.950 --> 00:34:09.410
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, sir, for joining us. Please continue.

asr-000079
00:34:09.730 --> 00:34:10.650
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Good afternoon, sir.

asr-000080
00:34:11.650 --> 00:34:22.130
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to our fiscal performance under the government auditing program, the COA was able to transmit to the audited agencies,

asr-000081
00:34:22.130 --> 00:34:24.590
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: the following reports.

asr-000082
00:34:25.250 --> 00:34:40.610
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For fiscal year 2025, 2,663 annual audit reports, 43 fraud audit reports, 10 special audit reports, and 3 performance audit reports.

asr-000083
00:34:40.610 --> 00:34:50.350
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For the first semester of fiscal year 2026, 2,605 annual audit reports, 10 fraud audit reports,

asr-000084
00:34:50.350 --> 00:34:56.210
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: 4 special audit reports, and 3 performance audit reports.

asr-000085
00:34:56.690 --> 00:35:05.380
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Still under the government auditing program, COA was able to publish in our COA website,

asr-000086
00:35:06.060 --> 00:35:10.420
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: the annual audit reports for fiscal year 2025.

asr-000087
00:35:11.540 --> 00:35:16.480
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: There were 2,255 annual audit reports.

asr-000088
00:35:16.480 --> 00:35:21.460
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For the first semester of fiscal year 2026, none.

asr-000089
00:35:21.720 --> 00:35:22.480
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Since the...

asr-000090
00:35:22.500 --> 00:35:31.120
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: The deadline of the transmittal of our annual audit reports to the audited agency was June 30.

asr-000091
00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:45.500
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And within 60 days from receipt of the COA annual audit report, the audit agencies are required to submit the status report on the actions taken on the audit observations and recommendations.

asr-000092
00:35:45.500 --> 00:35:52.460
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And this status report shall be published together with the annual audit reports.

asr-000093
00:35:52.500 --> 00:35:57.780
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: until October 31 of the year.

asr-000094
00:35:59.860 --> 00:36:11.960
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the government accountancy program, COA was able to submit reports to the Office of the President, House of Representatives, and Senate.

asr-000095
00:36:11.960 --> 00:36:15.960
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For 2025, we submitted...

asr-000096
00:36:16.680 --> 00:36:21.960
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: 2025 and 2026, we were able to transmit annual reports.

asr-000097
00:36:22.500 --> 00:36:27.300
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the report of appropriations, allotments, obligations, and disbursements.

asr-000098
00:36:27.860 --> 00:36:38.540
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the annual financial reports of local government, national government, and government corporations, we submitted for fiscal year 2025.

asr-000099
00:36:38.940 --> 00:36:44.400
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For 2026, our deadline for submission will be on September 30.

asr-000100
00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:52.840
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the government accountancy program, COA was able to issue...

asr-000101
00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:58.000
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Two circular, COA circulars for fiscal year 2025.

asr-000102
00:36:58.660 --> 00:37:04.700
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Two COA circulars for the first semester of first fiscal year 2026.

asr-000103
00:37:04.700 --> 00:37:19.720
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the agency users trained and assisted, for fiscal year 2025, we were able to train 3,817 users.

asr-000104
00:37:19.720 --> 00:37:23.720
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And for the first semester of fiscal year 2026,

asr-000105
00:37:24.460 --> 00:37:29.320
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: we were able to train 2,148 agency users.

asr-000106
00:37:29.340 --> 00:37:33.060
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: As to the government financial adjudication program,

asr-000107
00:37:33.060 --> 00:37:34.040
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: for fiscal year 2025,

asr-000108
00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:43.600
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: there were 811 cases decided by the Commission proper,

asr-000109
00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:48.480
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: 587 cases by the national government audit sector,

asr-000110
00:37:48.480 --> 00:37:53.600
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: 188 cases for the corporate government audit sector,

asr-000116
00:37:53.600 --> 00:38:02.560
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: and 571 cases for the local government audit sector. For the first semester

asr-000117
00:38:02.560 --> 00:38:12.600
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: of fiscal year 2026, 448 cases were decided by the Commission proper, 116 cases by the national

asr-000118
00:38:12.600 --> 00:38:21.120
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: government audit sector, 42 by the corporate government audit sector, and 224 cases for the

asr-000119
00:38:21.120 --> 00:38:30.720
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: local government sector. As to our budget under the fiscal year 2027 national expenditure program,

asr-000120
00:38:30.720 --> 00:38:43.100
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: we have as approved under the NEP of $16,046,527,000 to be exact.

asr-000121
00:38:44.640 --> 00:38:52.500
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And this consists of the agency-specific budget,

asr-000122
00:38:52.620 --> 00:39:02.620
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: of $14.77 billion, and retirement and life insurance premium of $1.272 billion.

asr-000123
00:39:03.820 --> 00:39:16.760
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Out of this, for the agency-specific budget, it consists of the personal services of $14.036 billion

asr-000124
00:39:16.760 --> 00:39:22.420
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: and $737.977 million.

asr-000125
00:39:23.420 --> 00:39:27.580
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So we have no capital outlay.

asr-000126
00:39:27.720 --> 00:39:37.060
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So the last slide is the comparative data between the NEP as against our budget proposal

asr-000127
00:39:37.060 --> 00:39:39.160
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000128
00:39:39.880 --> 00:39:48.060
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For the personal services, there is an increase of 1.17%.

asr-000129
00:39:48.060 --> 00:39:52.260
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: And this is due to the increase in our authorized

asr-000130
00:39:52.620 --> 00:39:58.900
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: plantilla positions, and inclusion of the fourth tranche of the Salary Standardization Law.

asr-000131
00:39:59.540 --> 00:40:09.380
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Then for the MOOE, 34.48% decrease, and this is pertaining to the first year implementation

asr-000132
00:40:09.380 --> 00:40:18.740
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: of the COA ISSP, and additional funding for our citizen participatory audit, MOE requirements.

asr-000133
00:40:18.740 --> 00:40:26.280
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Then, zero for, I mean, 100% decrease for our capital outlay.

asr-000134
00:40:26.980 --> 00:40:30.900
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So, that's all for the presentation. Thank you very much.

asr-000135
00:40:31.360 --> 00:40:38.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Assistant Commissioner Nilda Plaras. I'll ask my colleague, Senator Tulfo, our

asr-000136
00:40:38.820 --> 00:40:43.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Blue Ribbon Chair, if he might have a statement or some queries.

asr-000137
00:40:43.620 --> 00:40:46.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Just a few quick questions.

asr-000138
00:40:46.100 --> 00:40:55.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Chair, una po sa lahat kay ASCOM Plaras, ba't wala pong capital outlay? I noticed.

asr-000139
00:40:56.620 --> 00:40:59.560
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Wala po sa NEP, although we proposed.

asr-000140
00:40:59.820 --> 00:41:01.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Magkano po yung proposal po ninyo?

asr-000141
00:41:02.340 --> 00:41:09.450
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: 1.177 billion.

asr-000142
00:41:09.830 --> 00:41:12.230
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Billion. Para saan po ito? Ano po ang purpose sana?

asr-000143
00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:22.770
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: For the capital outlay, we have the building and other structures.

asr-000144
