COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: almost 50% of that

asr-002091
01:44:39.820 --> 01:44:41.760
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: or 45% to be exact

asr-002092
01:44:41.760 --> 01:44:44.000
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: ay nasa Bulacan po.

asr-002093
01:44:44.680 --> 01:44:45.740
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, dun po talaga kami

asr-002094
01:44:45.740 --> 01:44:48.000
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: nag-concentrate. So, as of

asr-002095
01:44:48.000 --> 01:44:50.120
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: today, nagkaroon po kami

asr-002096
01:44:50.120 --> 01:44:50.560
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: ng...

asr-002097
01:44:50.560 --> 01:44:53.900
Senator Joel Villanueva: How many projects? Kung ilan po ito?

asr-002097-split-2
01:44:53.900 --> 01:44:54.980
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Marami po ito.

asr-002098
01:44:55.620 --> 01:44:56.020
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Marami.

asr-002099
01:44:56.100 --> 01:44:57.960
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Marami po ito. But so far

asr-002100
01:44:57.960 --> 01:44:59.800
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: ang fraud audit po namin, tuloy-tuloy

asr-002101
01:44:59.800 --> 01:44:59.940
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: naman.

asr-002102
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:02.180
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So far, nasa almost 50 na po kami.

asr-002103
01:45:02.860 --> 01:45:03.660
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Almost 50.

asr-002104
01:45:03.800 --> 01:45:05.860
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: And then, iba-iba po yung nakita namin.

asr-002105
01:45:06.020 --> 01:45:10.300
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: But marami po sa kanila talagang defective or non-existent.

asr-002106
01:45:10.520 --> 01:45:16.440
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, yun po ang aming naging conclusion doon sa fraud audit.

asr-002107
01:45:16.520 --> 01:45:18.740
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, we issued notice of disallowances.

asr-002108
01:45:19.420 --> 01:45:25.140
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: And we already submitted this to the Office of the Ombudsman.

asr-002109
01:45:25.140 --> 01:45:30.220
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Dati po, nung nandiyan pa po yung ICI, we submitted the ICI to the Office of the Ombudsman also.

asr-002110
01:45:31.020 --> 01:45:35.540
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Now, doon po kasi sa mga NDs that we issued and sa flood control projects,

asr-002111
01:45:35.540 --> 01:45:40.700
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: meron po kasi dyan tinatawag na persons liable.

asr-002112
01:45:41.820 --> 01:45:47.840
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, makikita po namin, we can submit it to you, we can submit it to the Honorable Finance Committee.

asr-002113
01:45:48.720 --> 01:45:51.120
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: At makikita po nyo yung mga persons liable, nandoon naman po.

asr-002114
01:45:51.240 --> 01:45:54.860
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: It's really the DPWH people yung po nag-i-implement.

asr-002115
01:45:54.860 --> 01:45:59.540
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Because it's the budget of the DPWH and it's their personnel po sa Bulacan.

asr-002116
01:46:00.020 --> 01:46:05.960
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Wala naman po si Sen. Joel doon at hindi naman siya implement or he's a legislator.

asr-002117
01:46:06.640 --> 01:46:16.000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Would you know if there are projects being pushed by politicians in these particular areas na inaudit ninyo?

asr-002118
01:46:16.420 --> 01:46:18.300
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Wala po kaming nakikita eh.

asr-002119
01:46:18.440 --> 01:46:22.900
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: But what we see is yung implementing agency which is the DPWH po.

asr-002120
01:46:22.900 --> 01:46:25.920
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Nasa JA po kasi yun.

asr-002121
01:46:25.940 --> 01:46:33.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: Can we also ask, dito sa 50 fraudulent, I mean 50 fraud audits, yung breakdown po binabanggit nyo,

asr-002122
01:46:33.860 --> 01:46:38.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: some were ghosts, some were, do we have a breakdown already?

asr-002123
01:46:38.560 --> 01:46:49.560
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung ilan doon yung talagang ghosts, yung ilan doon yung substandard, extremely substandard materials yung ginamit?

asr-002124
01:46:49.560 --> 01:46:52.080
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: We don't have it right now but we can submit po.

asr-002125
01:46:52.900 --> 01:46:54.780
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So far po, majority po, wala po siya.

asr-002126
01:46:55.220 --> 01:47:03.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: With the indulgence of Sen. Villanueva, siguro Chairman Lielo, we would like to, can you submit to the committee

asr-002127
01:47:03.540 --> 01:47:12.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung list ng inyo pong investigation on which projects are found to be irregular, yung pong may ghosts,

asr-002128
01:47:12.420 --> 01:47:22.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: or basta hindi po substandard because our policy right now in this budget hearings is to resume flood

asr-002129
01:47:22.900 --> 01:47:26.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: control projects to complete the uncompleted ones.

asr-002130
01:47:26.380 --> 01:47:29.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi nakita naman natin ang naging epekto ngayon.

asr-002131
01:47:29.320 --> 01:47:39.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Because for 2026 talagang ziniro, flood control, ang nangyari tuloy talagang may mga puwang, may mga gaps, mga uncompleted.

asr-002132
01:47:39.860 --> 01:47:44.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So which were said, kasi naipon mo yung tubig pero puwapasok naman yung tubig.

asr-002133
01:47:44.960 --> 01:47:52.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So our instruction is also to complete the uncompleted projects, tapusin yung mga dapat tapusin, close the gap,

asr-002134
01:47:52.900 --> 01:48:00.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but we would want a list of these projects which we would, yung inyo pong nag-undergo ng investigation

asr-002135
01:48:00.860 --> 01:48:12.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which are found to be fraudulent, yung pong substandard para po sa amin pong pag-review

asr-002136
01:48:12.000 --> 01:48:17.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and then we will only allow those uncompleted projects that are not irregular or fraudulent.

asr-002137
01:48:17.180 --> 01:48:22.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So we appreciate the submission of this investigation.

asr-002138
01:48:22.900 --> 01:48:26.600
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: We commit to submit that, Your Honor.

asr-002139
01:48:26.700 --> 01:48:33.360
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Lahat po ng aming fraud audit reports, we'll also summarize it po para po mas madali makita.

asr-002140
01:48:33.860 --> 01:48:38.900
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: And at the same time, we'll also submit the report na comprehensive per item.

asr-002141
01:48:40.040 --> 01:48:45.900
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Idagdag ko lang din po na as early as 2016, Your Honors, the Commission Audit in charge of the DPWH

asr-002142
01:48:45.900 --> 01:48:51.900
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: has already issued an observation po na wala po kasing...

asr-002143
01:48:52.900 --> 01:48:56.380
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: master plan yung pong paggawa ng pong flood control.

asr-002144
01:48:56.560 --> 01:49:00.740
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So kumbaga po kanya-kanya po siya, but I think it has to be closed.

asr-002145
01:49:00.860 --> 01:49:02.560
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Tama po kayo, nagkaroon ng gaps eh.

asr-002146
01:49:02.660 --> 01:49:03.940
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So kasi po wala master plan.

asr-002147
01:49:04.700 --> 01:49:08.480
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So there has to be a master plan and para lahat po nakasarado.

asr-002148
01:49:08.660 --> 01:49:11.320
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Otherwise po, ang nangyari po kasi...

asr-002149
01:49:11.320 --> 01:49:21.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sir, I'm a witness. My colleague here has been ranting about this year in and year out ever since 3-4 years ago.

asr-002150
01:49:21.400 --> 01:49:25.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang problema talaga, we were going back.

asr-002151
01:49:26.080 --> 01:49:31.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I had a post 2014 on the importance of a master plan for all projects.

asr-002152
01:49:31.960 --> 01:49:41.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi lang flood control, but I have been advocating a master plan for infrastructure and national development

asr-002153
01:49:41.060 --> 01:49:45.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which would include transport modernization, yung sa power, sa energy.

asr-002154
01:49:45.940 --> 01:49:50.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasaba na rin po yung water management and flood control.

asr-002155
01:49:50.740 --> 01:49:51.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang nangyari dito...

asr-002156
01:49:51.280 --> 01:49:51.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang nangyari dito...

asr-002157
01:49:51.400 --> 01:49:56.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, Chairman Liel, yung ibang projects, sorry na lang po.

asr-002158
01:49:56.600 --> 01:50:03.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kahit walang Regional Development Council approval, kahit wala sa master plan, kahit walang convergence, kahit hindi kailangan,

asr-002159
01:50:03.760 --> 01:50:06.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: talagang isinagawa para pagkakitaan.

asr-002160
01:50:06.160 --> 01:50:09.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mukhang gano'n na lumalabas, lalo rin sa mga nag-ghost.

asr-002161
01:50:09.640 --> 01:50:14.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So in order, I think we would need your [unclear].

asr-002162
01:50:16.260 --> 01:50:21.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You'll be a big factor in how we will be able to bring back that confidence

asr-002163
01:50:21.280 --> 01:50:25.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and trust, especially in this budget season, by providing us with this list.

asr-002164
01:50:26.080 --> 01:50:27.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung pong hinihingi na api kanina.

asr-002165
01:50:27.560 --> 01:50:29.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tsaka yung pong, siguro yung pong isa tungkol sa master plan.

asr-002166
01:50:30.540 --> 01:50:36.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Do you think, Chairman Liel, that in case we push itong talagang may master plan pa,

asr-002167
01:50:36.080 --> 01:50:44.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: this will definitely prevent occurrence of projects that are not needed and are intended only to, alam nyo na,

asr-002168
01:50:45.300 --> 01:50:47.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to enrich some people's pockets.

asr-002169
01:50:48.220 --> 01:50:49.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi kailangan eh.

asr-002170
01:50:49.040 --> 01:50:51.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So what are what we want now?

asr-002171
01:50:51.280 --> 01:50:57.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We want RDC approval or at least a provincial approval to make sure that these projects are needed.

asr-002172
01:50:58.280 --> 01:51:00.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi yung basta lang po project eh para pagkakitaan.

asr-002173
01:51:01.060 --> 01:51:07.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So I'm asking your guidance also and what you think na amin pong sinasagawa.

asr-002174
01:51:07.680 --> 01:51:08.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ito po yung hinihingi natin.

asr-002175
01:51:09.200 --> 01:51:18.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: RDC approval, program of works, tapos basta po nasa flood-prone, top 10 flood-prone provinces

asr-002176
01:51:18.140 --> 01:51:20.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: or it can be used as justification.

asr-002177
01:51:21.280 --> 01:51:28.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There are 18 major river basins in the absence of a master plan.

asr-002178
01:51:28.220 --> 01:51:35.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So siguro these are the considerations that we would have in order for us to approve flood control projects this time.

asr-002179
01:51:36.600 --> 01:51:37.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So yung pong ano namin.

asr-002180
01:51:37.460 --> 01:51:39.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, ano na po, your thoughts, Chairperson?

asr-002181
01:51:39.940 --> 01:51:42.500
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: We agree po, Your Honors.

asr-002182
01:51:42.500 --> 01:51:49.560
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Actually, sabi ko nga po sa inyo, as early as 2016, nag-issue na po ng observation ng Commission on Audit on that.

asr-002183
01:51:50.160 --> 01:51:50.500
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: And just to mention...

asr-002184
01:51:51.280 --> 01:51:58.580
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: I understand when you were mayor po of San Juan, kasi dati po ang San Juan binabahat.

asr-002185
01:51:58.700 --> 01:52:02.480
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So I think when you were there, marami po kayong nagawa, kaya po nabawasan ito ng...

asr-002186
01:52:02.480 --> 01:52:10.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, siguro, if flood control, if done right, can really be effective.

asr-002187
01:52:10.920 --> 01:52:12.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Not to...

asr-002188
01:52:13.800 --> 01:52:17.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi ko naman siya inaangat sa sarili.

asr-002189
01:52:17.320 --> 01:52:20.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But you know, ano to, sinasabi ko, Sen. Villanueva, ano yung sa Navotas,

asr-002190
01:52:21.280 --> 01:52:24.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: under, ano to, below sea level.

asr-002191
01:52:25.620 --> 01:52:35.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero by placing strategic pumping stations in strategic areas, natanggal nila Toby Tiangco yung baha.

asr-002192
01:52:36.060 --> 01:52:37.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Naginaya po namin sa San Juan.

asr-002193
01:52:38.120 --> 01:52:42.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We have about five or six barangays that are low-lying areas.

asr-002194
01:52:42.740 --> 01:52:47.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Basin, na kahit dalawang linggo nang walang ulan, baha pa rin.

asr-002195
01:52:47.260 --> 01:52:49.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dati, 15 to 20 feet, ang lalim.

asr-002196
01:52:49.320 --> 01:52:51.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero ngayon, halos na wala.

asr-002197
01:52:51.280 --> 01:52:54.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Unfortunately, may isa na lang doon na naiwan, na inirata.

asr-002198
01:52:55.080 --> 01:52:58.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Na nirequest ko kay Bonoan at kay Bernardo noon na hindi pinagbigyan.

asr-002199
01:52:58.900 --> 01:53:01.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ayaw kasi nung congressman namin dahil ayaw nung mayor.

asr-002200
01:53:02.320 --> 01:53:04.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So may isa na lang doon nababaha.

asr-002201
01:53:04.240 --> 01:53:06.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kung meron, yun na lang yung naiwan doon.

asr-002202
01:53:06.980 --> 01:53:12.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So sabi ako, nagkiusap ko sa DPWH sila na kung ano pa mangyari, basta gawin nyo na lang.

asr-002203
01:53:13.200 --> 01:53:17.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So thank you for that, for yung pong sa San Juan na mention nyo.

asr-002204
01:53:17.700 --> 01:53:20.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And I think it was the Navotas that we followed.

asr-002205
01:53:21.280 --> 01:53:25.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Naging yung Bombastik pumps nila na kami pong ginaya.

asr-002206
01:53:25.180 --> 01:53:25.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-002207
01:53:26.220 --> 01:53:27.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sige po, please continue.

asr-002208
01:53:27.820 --> 01:53:28.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: San Juan.

asr-002209
01:53:28.560 --> 01:53:30.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002210
01:53:30.720 --> 01:53:38.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: And let me put on record that I am a living testimony of what you have been espousing here in the Senate.

asr-002211
01:53:38.380 --> 01:53:47.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: And since the time you were the mayor of the great city of San Juan, yung pinupush po ninyo na master plan.

asr-002212
01:53:47.740 --> 01:53:51.240
Senator Joel Villanueva: At you're not only supporting me with the master plan ng flood control.

asr-002213
01:53:51.280 --> 01:53:57.800
Senator Joel Villanueva: But yun nga po, ako, lagi akong supportive doon sa mga gusto nyo yung mga infrastructure projects,

asr-002214
01:53:57.900 --> 01:54:01.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: especially doon sa transportation, sa railways, etc.

asr-002215
01:54:01.500 --> 01:54:08.280
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kaya mapalad kayo, Senator JV, at nagawan ng paraan yung San Juan.

asr-002216
01:54:08.700 --> 01:54:14.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: At kami hanggang ngayon sa Bulacan, still suffering.

asr-002217
01:54:15.900 --> 01:54:21.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Literally, figuratively, physically, mentally, and sometimes spiritually.

asr-002218
01:54:21.260 --> 01:54:35.460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. Chairman, just to put on record, Mr. Chairman, and I'd like to give this information to our COA family headed by Chairman Cordoba.

asr-002219
01:54:36.080 --> 01:54:43.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung po sa amin sa Bulacan, for example, doon sa Paumbong, sa Paumbong, sa Barangay Cruz,

asr-002220
01:54:43.040 --> 01:54:51.170
Senator Joel Villanueva: tsaka Barangay Masukol, eh hindi na po baha yung problema nila.

asr-002221
01:54:51.350 --> 01:54:53.310
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi nasanay na po sila.

asr-002222
01:54:53.530 --> 01:54:59.990
Senator Joel Villanueva: Na hanggang dibdib, lagpas tao, at kahit summer, bumabaha po sa kanila.

asr-002223
01:55:00.450 --> 01:55:07.010
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang problema po nila ngayon, unti-unti nang kinakain nung dagat, yung lupa, nung barangay.

asr-002224
01:55:07.450 --> 01:55:14.310
Senator Joel Villanueva: Itong Barangay Santa Cruz, tsaka Barangay Masukol, about 3,000 siguro yung mga residents po dyan.

asr-002225
01:55:14.590 --> 01:55:19.090
Senator Joel Villanueva: At unfortunately, sabi nga nila, hindi na yung baha problema namin.

asr-002226
01:55:19.230 --> 01:55:21.830
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi kinakain na ng lupa, mabuburan na kami sa mapa.

asr-002227
01:55:21.830 --> 01:55:28.790
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ganon din po yung kalagayan sa Hagonoy, Bulacan, sa Barangay Pugad at Barangay Tibagin.

asr-002228
01:55:28.930 --> 01:55:31.350
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ano naman yung nangyari dito sa dalawang barangay na ito?

asr-002229
01:55:32.030 --> 01:55:39.590
Senator Joel Villanueva: Before the fiasco, before this erupted, the kasuklam-suklam na mga pangyayari about flood control,

asr-002230
01:55:40.450 --> 01:55:47.010
Senator Joel Villanueva: meron pong breakwater at seawall dyan sa dalawang barangay na yan.

asr-002231
01:55:48.450 --> 01:55:49.390
Senator Joel Villanueva: Meron na po siya.

asr-002232
01:55:49.390 --> 01:55:58.350
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero dahil gagawin at palalakihin, patitibayin, i-strengthenin yung seawall, binakbak na po nila.

asr-002233
01:55:58.470 --> 01:56:00.130
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sisimulan na eh, gagawin na po.

asr-002234
01:56:00.630 --> 01:56:04.450
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nung gagawin na po, natigil lahat ngayon ng flood control.

asr-002235
01:56:04.970 --> 01:56:05.950
Senator Joel Villanueva: So ano nangyari?

asr-002236
01:56:06.350 --> 01:56:19.030
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nung binakbak, nasira lalo dahil bawal ang flood control, dahil maraming siraulong kurakot na dapat dyan.

asr-002237
01:56:19.030 --> 01:56:24.990
Senator Joel Villanueva: Talagang ako, fight ako sa firing squad eh, sa mga taong ganyan eh.

asr-002238
01:56:26.610 --> 01:56:28.150
Senator Joel Villanueva: Eh, hindi po ginawa.

asr-002239
01:56:28.390 --> 01:56:37.090
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nung hindi po ginawa, hanggang ngayon ho, ilang taon na, na wala ho ni Pondo or anything, Mr. Chairman, wala ho at hindi na gagawa.

asr-002240
01:56:37.830 --> 01:56:41.210
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nagsimula na rin pong kainin ng dagat yung lupa.

asr-002241
01:56:41.810 --> 01:56:46.450
Senator Joel Villanueva: To cut the story short, ito hong mga barangay na ito, sa barangay Paumbong,

asr-002242
01:56:47.150 --> 01:56:48.350
Senator Joel Villanueva: at barangay...

asr-002243
01:56:48.350 --> 01:56:52.470
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ah, dun po sa bayan ng Paumbong, barangay Santa Cruz, barangay Masukol,

asr-002244
01:56:52.890 --> 01:56:56.150
Senator Joel Villanueva: sa Hagunoy, barangay Pugat, barangay Tibagin, sa Hagunoy.

asr-002245
01:56:56.730 --> 01:56:58.250
Senator Joel Villanueva: Eh, hindi na po problema nila yung ba.

asr-002246
01:56:58.330 --> 01:57:02.570
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang problema nila, mawawala na po sa mapa yung kanilang mga barangay.

asr-002247
01:57:03.090 --> 01:57:06.450
Senator Joel Villanueva: There's one in barangay, Mr. Chairman, in Hagunoy,

asr-002248
01:57:06.930 --> 01:57:12.310
Senator Joel Villanueva: na I have to call the attention of the DPWH Secretary because

asr-002249
01:57:12.310 --> 01:57:16.070
Senator Joel Villanueva: I forgot the name of barangay.

asr-002250
01:57:16.070 --> 01:57:17.270
Senator Joel Villanueva: I think Santa Cruz also.

asr-002251
01:57:17.270 --> 01:57:25.230
Senator Joel Villanueva: In Hagunoy, meron naman po doon kasama doon sa problema na may kaso.

asr-002252
01:57:26.370 --> 01:57:29.390
Senator Joel Villanueva: And according to them, may gate po eh, may gate.

asr-002253
01:57:29.510 --> 01:57:32.350
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi ho magamit yung gate. Bumabaha na po.

asr-002254
01:57:32.470 --> 01:57:36.870
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dahil ang sabi lang daw ay hindi po pwedeng galawin yan dahil may kaso yan.

asr-002255
01:57:38.230 --> 01:57:45.410
Senator Joel Villanueva: The good thing, I don't know the real situation and ayokong makialam doon sa mga kaso-kasong ganyan

asr-002256
01:57:45.410 --> 01:57:47.190
Senator Joel Villanueva: dahil ngayon pag nakialam,

asr-002257
01:57:47.270 --> 01:57:48.370
Senator Joel Villanueva: kaya nadadamay ka eh.

asr-002258
01:57:50.130 --> 01:57:56.090
Senator Joel Villanueva: Si Secretary Vince, nagutos right away, the next day ho, naggalaw po yung gate.

asr-002259
01:57:56.550 --> 01:58:01.730
Senator Joel Villanueva: I don't know kung nakipag-coordinate po yata sa COA or other agencies in the government.

asr-002260
01:58:01.870 --> 01:58:04.470
Senator Joel Villanueva: But thanks to Sec. Vince, naggalaw po yun.

asr-002261
01:58:04.990 --> 01:58:06.310
Senator Joel Villanueva: Malaking naging ginhawa.

asr-002262
01:58:06.790 --> 01:58:09.150
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi imagine, yung gate lang, ibababa lang po, di ba?

asr-002263
01:58:10.150 --> 01:58:12.510
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dahil lang daw po may kaso, hindi po ginawa.

asr-002264
01:58:12.510 --> 01:58:16.510
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, nag-suffer yung buong barangay.

asr-002265
01:58:17.270 --> 01:58:19.870
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yun lang po yung mga maliliit na bagay na gano'n.

asr-002266
01:58:19.990 --> 01:58:23.650
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I hope, ang COA naman natin, hindi naman in the box yan.

asr-002267
01:58:23.750 --> 01:58:28.170
Senator Joel Villanueva: I don't think yung COA natin, extremist yung mga COA auditors natin

asr-002268
01:58:28.170 --> 01:58:36.490
Senator Joel Villanueva: para yung mga ganitong bagay na ito, hindi matulungan yung mga kababayan po natin.

asr-002269
01:58:36.570 --> 01:58:41.750
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, yun lang po, Mr. Chairman, gusto kong ipaabot sa ating mga kasama sa COA

asr-002270
01:58:41.750 --> 01:58:46.430
Senator Joel Villanueva: na malaking tulong ang kailangan ng mga kababayan natin.

asr-002271
01:58:46.430 --> 01:58:50.770
Senator Joel Villanueva: Lalo na po doon sa mga apektado ng baha.

asr-002272
01:58:51.530 --> 01:58:58.810
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dahil nakakasunog ang apoy, hindi na po tayo magluluto at papatayin natin sa gutom yung ating mga kababayan.

asr-002273
01:58:59.130 --> 01:59:06.430
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm really not happy na wala hong flood control the past year program kahit na ito'y nararapat.

asr-002274
01:59:07.370 --> 01:59:08.850
Senator Joel Villanueva: And records will bail me out.

asr-002275
01:59:09.590 --> 01:59:14.650
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi ako sumuporta sa mga flood control programs because hindi ko nakikita na ito'y integrated

asr-002276
01:59:14.650 --> 01:59:16.350
Senator Joel Villanueva: at may master plan.

asr-002277
01:59:16.430 --> 01:59:17.490
Senator Joel Villanueva: That's the only reason.

asr-002278
01:59:17.490 --> 01:59:25.750
Senator Joel Villanueva: And these committees in the Senate, mga senador nakasama ko at mga nakatrabaho ko,

asr-002279
01:59:25.870 --> 01:59:31.450
Senator Joel Villanueva: alam po yung dahilan kung bakit ganito yung aking adhikain dito sa usapin nito.

asr-002280
01:59:31.530 --> 01:59:32.510
Senator Joel Villanueva: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-002281
01:59:33.130 --> 01:59:34.570
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Villanueva.

asr-002282
01:59:35.270 --> 01:59:41.490
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, sa totoo lang, that's why we wanted also to resume the flood control projects.

asr-002283
01:59:42.370 --> 01:59:43.710
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The uncompleted one, that is.

asr-002284
01:59:43.710 --> 01:59:45.710
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Because we have seen that...

asr-002285
01:59:46.430 --> 01:59:49.170
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dito sa monsoon rains, wala pa ngang bagyo ito.

asr-002286
01:59:49.710 --> 01:59:54.970
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tuloy-tuloy na ulan, lubog ang Metro Manila, lubog ang Bulacan, lubog ang Pampanga, hanggang Tarlac.

asr-002287
01:59:55.770 --> 01:59:56.710
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ano eh.

asr-002288
01:59:57.350 --> 01:59:59.950
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, iba na rin talaga yung climate change.

asr-002289
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:09.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But still, we need to resume the flood-mitigating projects, especially the complete, the uncompleted.

asr-002290
02:00:09.720 --> 02:00:16.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro wala namang masama roon, Chairman, di ba, as long as these projects are not found to be irregular or substandard.

asr-002291
02:00:17.700 --> 02:00:27.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think this will be more beneficial as it would prevent the further suffering of the people in Bulacan and Pampanga and even Metro Manila and Tarlac.

asr-002292
02:00:27.880 --> 02:00:35.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At least kung ma-mitigate natin, mabawasan natin yung pagbabaha, masara natin yung gaps, kasi mas masama yung may puwang eh.

asr-002293
02:00:36.020 --> 02:00:38.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tubig yan. Maghahanap talaga ng papasukan yan.

asr-002294
02:00:38.440 --> 02:00:42.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tapos pinipigilan mo namang mawala yung tubig para mawala yung baha.

asr-002295
02:00:42.660 --> 02:00:45.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So parang naging ano siya.

asr-002296
02:00:45.700 --> 02:00:48.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So ang ano natin is to close the gaps.

asr-002297
02:00:48.800 --> 02:00:55.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And also, if I would, magsimula tayo, Senator Villanueva, yung NIA and DPWH.

asr-002298
02:00:55.680 --> 02:00:56.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dapat dito,

asr-002299
02:00:56.220 --> 02:01:00.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in the absence of a master plan, convergence na.

asr-002300
02:01:00.760 --> 02:01:04.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then sa taas pa lang dapat meron nang water impounding.

asr-002301
02:01:05.940 --> 02:01:10.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tapos nakaano yan ng flood control, water impounding.

asr-002302
02:01:10.940 --> 02:01:12.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi pag tag-ulan, sobra-sobra ulan natin.

asr-002303
02:01:13.080 --> 02:01:14.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pag tagtuyot naman, walang-wala tayo, di ba?

asr-002304
02:01:15.760 --> 02:01:22.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So I think we should change yung view, yung view eh na yung tubig hindi dapat perwisyo.

asr-002305
02:01:22.240 --> 02:01:24.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dapat treated as a resource.

asr-002306
02:01:24.060 --> 02:01:25.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero gawin natin.

asr-002307
02:01:26.220 --> 02:01:29.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kailangan natin ng tamang flood water management, I think.

asr-002308
02:01:29.400 --> 02:01:32.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yun ang atin pong direksyon, di ba?

asr-002309
02:01:33.140 --> 02:01:34.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sige, Chairperson Cordoba.

asr-002310
02:01:35.060 --> 02:01:37.200
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Thank you for, salamat po sa lahat ng binanggit ninyo.

asr-002311
02:01:37.740 --> 02:01:42.700
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Actually po, Your Honors, if may mga kailangan po na i-cover sila DPWH,

asr-002312
02:01:42.940 --> 02:01:45.280
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: kagaya po nung binabanggit ninyo, kasi may kaso, hindi pwedeng gawin.

asr-002313
02:01:45.400 --> 02:01:51.520
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Kung kailangan po, we're willing to sit down on an item per item with the DPWH.

asr-002314
02:01:51.640 --> 02:01:52.560
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: And actually, we're doing it po.

asr-002315
02:01:53.400 --> 02:01:54.860
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Pagka po may mga question sila,

asr-002316
02:01:54.860 --> 02:01:56.200
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: tinutulungan namin sila para

asr-002317
02:01:56.320 --> 02:02:04.440
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: magawa po nila kahit po may mga pending na kaso, pending na mga legalities.

asr-002318
02:02:04.660 --> 02:02:07.380
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: But importante po yung public service ay tuloy-tuloy.

asr-002319
02:02:07.540 --> 02:02:08.720
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Hindi po siya dapat huminto.

asr-002320
02:02:08.980 --> 02:02:09.400
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Salamat po.

asr-002321
02:02:10.920 --> 02:02:12.060
Senator Joel Villanueva: One last issue.

asr-002322
02:02:12.880 --> 02:02:17.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: If there's nothing more about the flood control program.

asr-002323
02:02:17.040 --> 02:02:22.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tinitingnan ko lang po kasi itong COA's Technical Services and Systems Audit Subprogram

asr-002324
02:02:23.280 --> 02:02:26.080
Senator Joel Villanueva: that targets only 18 ISIT audit or

asr-002325
02:02:26.200 --> 02:02:37.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: evaluation reports in 2027. Is that level of coverage sufficient given government's accelerating digitalization

asr-002326
02:02:37.520 --> 02:02:41.800
Senator Joel Villanueva: and growing cybersecurity and information system risk?

asr-002327
02:02:42.920 --> 02:02:49.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nakita ko lang ho yung 2027 target, 18 ISIT audit or evaluation reports.

asr-002328
02:02:51.920 --> 02:02:52.980
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Sandali lang po.

asr-002329
02:02:53.160 --> 02:02:53.960
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sige, please.

asr-002330
02:02:53.960 --> 02:02:54.960
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Yes, sorry.

asr-002331
02:02:57.640 --> 02:03:06.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: We just want to be clarified on this, how it prioritizes systems for audit and whether existing personnel

asr-002332
02:03:06.600 --> 02:03:14.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: and technology ay sufficient po dito to cover yung high-risk government information systems?

asr-002333
02:03:15.060 --> 02:03:18.280
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Thank you for the question, Mr. Chair, Sen. Villanueva.

asr-002334
02:03:18.720 --> 02:03:21.860
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Si Ascom Isidro po ang sasagot po.

asr-002335
02:03:22.440 --> 02:03:22.760
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Thank you.

asr-002336
02:03:22.760 --> 02:03:26.500
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair and Sen. Villanueva.

asr-002337
02:03:26.500 --> 02:03:27.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Please proceed.

asr-002338
02:03:27.640 --> 02:03:54.350
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: We have an office called the Internal Information Technology Audit Office under the Systems and Technical Services sector that does the IS audit and IT technical evaluation of procurement contracts and other contracts.

asr-002339
02:03:54.350 --> 02:03:59.710
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: At present, we have only 64 warm bodies.

asr-002340
02:04:00.550 --> 02:04:12.910
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: But ideally, the office needs 164 manpower with an existing approved plantelia of 81 plantelia positions.

asr-002341
02:04:12.910 --> 02:04:29.510
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: And these 64 warm bodies consist of auditors and administrative personnel, including...

asr-002342
02:04:29.510 --> 02:04:31.510
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: We also have...

asr-002343
02:04:32.150 --> 02:04:34.410
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Certified Information Systems Auditor.

asr-002344
02:04:35.510 --> 02:04:51.190
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: We have Public Procurement Specialist, Certified Fraud Examiner, Certified Public Accountants, and other disciplines consisting the office.

asr-002345
02:04:51.190 --> 02:04:59.410
Senator Joel Villanueva: So ito, magandang problema yata ito, kasi you have 64 but you have 81 available.

asr-002346
02:05:00.470 --> 02:05:02.030
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tama ba yung pagkakaintindi ko, ma?am?

asr-002347
02:05:02.150 --> 02:05:02.370
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Yes po.

asr-002348
02:05:02.930 --> 02:05:03.430
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Yes po.

asr-002349
02:05:03.430 --> 02:05:04.530
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Per our record, ma?am.

asr-002350
02:05:04.530 --> 02:05:09.790
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero hindi ninyo ma-fill up at the same problem that you are talking about?

asr-002351
02:05:10.690 --> 02:05:18.090
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: For the Information Systems Auditors, there is a certain criteria that need to be satisfied.

asr-002352
02:05:18.390 --> 02:05:20.130
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: Like, they need to be...

asr-002353
02:05:20.130 --> 02:05:23.090
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm sure. I was the head of agency before.

asr-002354
02:05:23.530 --> 02:05:26.150
Senator Joel Villanueva: So hindi ma-satisfy yun, kaya hindi ma-fill up?

asr-002355
02:05:26.810 --> 02:05:29.190
COA Assistant Commissioner Lucila M. Isidro: At present po, hindi po ma-satisfy po.

asr-002356
02:05:29.670 --> 02:05:31.990
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yun yung dahilan kung bakit

asr-002357
02:05:31.990 --> 02:05:34.110
Senator Joel Villanueva: ko tinatanong yung questions ko kanina.

asr-002358
02:05:34.110 --> 02:05:38.430
Senator Joel Villanueva: Is there a way that we can somehow adjust?

asr-002359
02:05:39.430 --> 02:05:41.250
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yun talaga kasi yung kailangan?

asr-002360
02:05:41.890 --> 02:05:44.690
Senator Joel Villanueva: At wala talaga tayong makikita?

asr-002361
02:05:45.070 --> 02:05:47.130
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hahanap ba tayo sa Milky Way Galaxy?

asr-002362
02:05:49.010 --> 02:05:50.950
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mag-train tayo sa TESDA?

asr-002363
02:05:52.810 --> 02:05:56.950
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Your Honor, it's really...

asr-002364
02:05:58.030 --> 02:05:58.950
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: We are...

asr-002365
02:05:58.950 --> 02:05:59.270
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: We are...

asr-002366
02:05:59.270 --> 02:06:07.250
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Dependent po kasi talagang sa compliance ng administrative rules ng civil service.

asr-002367
02:06:07.730 --> 02:06:13.210
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: So, kaya nga po kasi nasa standardization law po kami under.

asr-002368
02:06:13.670 --> 02:06:18.130
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: So, we really need to follow yung system ranking oppositions.

asr-002369
02:06:18.990 --> 02:06:20.710
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: So, hindi po kami ka...

asr-002370
02:06:20.710 --> 02:06:23.150
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Yung higher levels po kasi, for example,

asr-002371
02:06:23.750 --> 02:06:26.350
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: as yung entry level is so low,

asr-002372
02:06:26.350 --> 02:06:28.310
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: pero you cannot hire po.

asr-002373
02:06:29.270 --> 02:06:38.430
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Maglulundag ka ng salary grades kasi that is against dun sa administrative rules po ng civil service.

asr-002374
02:06:38.430 --> 02:06:46.190
Senator Joel Villanueva: And that will be addressed dun sa binabanggit ni Chairman na panukalang batas na ipupush po namin.

asr-002375
02:06:46.370 --> 02:06:46.830
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Yes po.

asr-002376
02:06:47.030 --> 02:06:48.550
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: If we are to be exempted sa standardization.

asr-002377
02:06:48.550 --> 02:06:54.630
Senator Joel Villanueva: Because otherwise, kahit ilang Pasko yung dumating, hindi ninyo ma-fill up-an.

asr-002378
02:06:54.890 --> 02:06:57.990
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Yes, even po na meron ka talagang qualified.

asr-002379
02:06:57.990 --> 02:06:58.990
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: Yan yung mga hinaharap.

asr-002380
02:06:59.270 --> 02:07:04.790
COA Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabochan: At the bottom, hindi ko po makakapag more than three salary grades.

asr-002381
02:07:04.790 --> 02:07:07.290
Senator Joel Villanueva: I got that. I know where you're coming from.

asr-002382
02:07:07.470 --> 02:07:10.930
Senator Joel Villanueva: I experienced that personally when I was with TESDA.

asr-002383
02:07:11.470 --> 02:07:12.570
Senator Joel Villanueva: Anyway, one last.

asr-002384
02:07:14.050 --> 02:07:20.310
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung financial management, nakita ko lang COA's own 2025 audit.

asr-002385
02:07:20.710 --> 02:07:25.870
Senator Joel Villanueva: You identified accounting deficiencies involving approximately 5.1 billion pesos.

asr-002386
02:07:25.870 --> 02:07:28.870
Senator Joel Villanueva: What accounts for the scale of...

asr-002387
02:07:29.270 --> 02:07:32.710
Senator Joel Villanueva: of these deficiencies, and what corrective measures?

asr-002388
02:07:33.010 --> 02:07:39.530
Senator Joel Villanueva: May independent audit eh, in-identify various accounting deficiencies totaling 5.1 billion.

asr-002389
02:07:40.550 --> 02:07:46.130
Senator Joel Villanueva: The amount does not by itself mean funds siguro that were lost or misused.

asr-002390
02:07:46.670 --> 02:07:53.050
Senator Joel Villanueva: But it is significant enough to perhaps get an explanation what this is.

asr-002391
02:08:06.230 --> 02:08:09.030
Senator Joel Villanueva: I got this from our LBRMO.

asr-002392
02:08:10.250 --> 02:08:15.450
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sa page 17, number 4.

asr-002393
02:08:15.790 --> 02:08:24.250
Senator Joel Villanueva: Various accounting deficiencies noted amounted to 5.101 billion as at year-end.

asr-002394
02:08:27.390 --> 02:08:29.830
Senator Joel Villanueva: LBRMO. Dito po, sa Senado po ito.

asr-002395
02:08:30.930 --> 02:08:34.430
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kaya nung nakita ko, sabi ko i-raise ko ito eh.

asr-002396
02:08:34.490 --> 02:08:35.410
Senator Joel Villanueva: You're not aware of this?

asr-002397
02:08:35.590 --> 02:08:36.330
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Hindi po, your honor.

asr-002398
02:08:37.250 --> 02:08:37.690
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay.

asr-002399
02:08:38.890 --> 02:08:39.490
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay, I'll set it.

asr-002400
02:08:40.250 --> 02:08:50.660
Senator Joel Villanueva: This is part of the audit report ng COA.

asr-002401
02:08:55.060 --> 02:08:57.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Audit observation number 4.

asr-002402
02:08:58.520 --> 02:09:01.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: But anyway, I will just furnish a copy nito.

asr-002403
02:09:02.400 --> 02:09:02.740
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

asr-002404
02:09:02.760 --> 02:09:07.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just wanted to make sure that we'll be able to clarify this.

asr-002405
02:09:07.620 --> 02:09:09.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi nagulat lang ako dun sa 5 billion eh.

asr-002406
02:09:10.160 --> 02:09:14.820
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm sure wala namang meaning where they're...

asr-002407
02:09:14.820 --> 02:09:18.100
Senator Joel Villanueva: May misuse or loss of funds.

asr-002408
02:09:18.240 --> 02:09:21.180
Senator Joel Villanueva: It's just that I think we need to explain this further

asr-002409
02:09:21.180 --> 02:09:25.860
Senator Joel Villanueva: para lang maset natin yung high standards ng COA.

asr-002410
02:09:26.300 --> 02:09:27.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: Salamat, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002411
02:09:27.320 --> 02:09:28.060
Senator Joel Villanueva: That will be all.

asr-002412
02:09:28.280 --> 02:09:32.700
Senator Joel Villanueva: And again, let me put on record my sincerest thanks and gratitude

asr-002413
02:09:32.700 --> 02:09:38.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: to the men and women of COA for your service.

asr-002414
02:09:39.040 --> 02:09:42.740
Senator Joel Villanueva: And most of all, I'd like to put on record my full support

asr-002415
02:09:42.740 --> 02:09:43.700
Senator Joel Villanueva: for the...

asr-002416
02:09:44.820 --> 02:09:50.840
Senator Joel Villanueva: approval of this briefing so that we can proceed

asr-002417
02:09:50.840 --> 02:09:55.600
Senator Joel Villanueva: for plenary action of their budget, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002418
02:09:55.740 --> 02:09:56.100
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

asr-002419
02:09:56.460 --> 02:09:58.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Villanueva, for your support

asr-002420
02:09:58.680 --> 02:10:03.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to our Commission on Audit.

asr-002421
02:10:04.240 --> 02:10:06.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Alam mo, ang hirap ng Commission on Audit,

asr-002422
02:10:06.700 --> 02:10:09.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ang tingin sa mga auditor, madalas, kontrabida eh.

asr-002423
02:10:10.340 --> 02:10:12.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang pag nakikita ito, lalo ng mga LG,

asr-002424
02:10:12.400 --> 02:10:13.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: nako, ito na naman ito, mga kontrabida.

asr-002425
02:10:13.980 --> 02:10:14.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But you know, this...

asr-002426
02:10:14.820 --> 02:10:18.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Auditors, state auditors, provide the checks and balances.

asr-002427
02:10:19.180 --> 02:10:22.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Make sure that money is well spent in government, diba?

asr-002428
02:10:22.940 --> 02:10:25.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya kailangan namin kayo dito, especially in our...

asr-002429
02:10:25.340 --> 02:10:31.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in our trust to bring back the confidence of people in government, no?

asr-002430
02:10:31.380 --> 02:10:34.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Na napakalaking bagay, lalo na dito sa ating budgeting.

asr-002431
02:10:35.500 --> 02:10:38.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Before we end, I would like to ask some questions from our...

asr-002432
02:10:38.860 --> 02:10:42.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kasi iniinvolve namin yung civil society organizations, no?

asr-002433
02:10:43.980 --> 02:10:44.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So that...

asr-002434
02:10:44.820 --> 02:10:48.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ito mga watchdogs can help us because we cannot...

asr-002435
02:10:48.100 --> 02:10:53.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sabi ko, it's humanly impossible for us to appreciate everything

asr-002436
02:10:53.100 --> 02:10:55.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in so short a time during the budget season, no?

asr-002437
02:10:57.180 --> 02:11:01.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Gabundok yung ibang volumes yun na pinapadala, line items.

asr-002438
02:11:01.460 --> 02:11:05.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So we are involving the civil society organizations, watchdogs,

asr-002439
02:11:05.300 --> 02:11:06.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and everybody else.

asr-002440
02:11:06.820 --> 02:11:10.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pag may nakita sila na irregular, to let us know

asr-002441
02:11:10.020 --> 02:11:12.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: so that we can already confront the agencies, no?

asr-002442
02:11:12.540 --> 02:11:14.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So ito po, from the CSO,

asr-002443
02:11:14.820 --> 02:11:17.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: naging concerned po ng maraming CSOs and groups

asr-002444
02:11:17.640 --> 02:11:20.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: na nagmo-monitor ng budget process sa mga nakaraang taon

asr-002445
02:11:20.600 --> 02:11:24.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ang delays ng publication ng COA's annual audit reports,

asr-002446
02:11:25.320 --> 02:11:28.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: particularly for the fiscal year 2023

asr-002447
02:11:28.240 --> 02:11:31.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: at sa ibang agency sa fiscal year 2024.

asr-002448
02:11:32.280 --> 02:11:36.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To address this under Section 107 of the 2026 GAA

asr-002449
02:11:36.380 --> 02:11:42.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: sets an October 31 deadline for the publication of annual audit reports.

asr-002450
02:11:42.620 --> 02:11:44.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang tanong, kumusta po ang

asr-002451
02:11:44.820 --> 02:11:47.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: implementation nito? Have all fiscal year 2024

asr-002452
02:11:47.620 --> 02:11:51.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: annual audit reports already been published on your website?

asr-002453
02:11:52.580 --> 02:11:54.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Published na po. Okay. Complete.

asr-002454
02:11:55.540 --> 02:11:59.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ito pong, is it on track to make all 2025 naman po

asr-002455
02:11:59.500 --> 02:12:01.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: audit reports available by October 31.

asr-002456
02:12:02.620 --> 02:12:04.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, so ongoing.

asr-002457
02:12:04.620 --> 02:12:06.200
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Idagdag ko lang po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002458
02:12:06.200 --> 02:12:12.840
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Kasi nung 2023 for 2024, nakalagay po kasi sa GAA na December,

asr-002459
02:12:13.620 --> 02:12:14.640
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: end of December po.

asr-002460
02:12:14.820 --> 02:12:16.760
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Last day. Kaya po, na-delay din talaga.

asr-002461
02:12:17.000 --> 02:12:18.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So ngayon, October 31 na?

asr-002462
02:12:18.220 --> 02:12:19.260
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: October 31 na po.

asr-002463
02:12:19.860 --> 02:12:22.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa follow-up, Chairman, would it be feasible for COA

asr-002464
02:12:22.660 --> 02:12:25.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to publish the annual audit reports earlier?

asr-002465
02:12:25.700 --> 02:12:27.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang request nila, July 30,

asr-002466
02:12:27.580 --> 02:12:32.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: so that Congress will have sufficient time to consider the audit findings.

asr-002467
02:12:33.180 --> 02:12:37.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi during the budget process, wala pa yung ano nyo, October 31.

asr-002468
02:12:37.620 --> 02:12:40.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ang ano lang nila, kung kaya yung July 31,

asr-002469
02:12:40.760 --> 02:12:44.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: para po meron silang time to consider the audit findings.

asr-002470
02:12:44.820 --> 02:12:47.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: During the budget process, is it feasible?

asr-002471
02:12:49.460 --> 02:12:56.360
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: Sir, pursuant to Section 107 of the GAA 2027,

asr-002472
02:12:56.360 --> 02:13:01.940
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: may requirement kasi po, upon the receipt of the annual audit report

asr-002473
02:13:01.940 --> 02:13:06.840
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: by the audited agency, required sila to submit the status of actions taken

asr-002474
02:13:06.840 --> 02:13:09.360
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: on the audit observations and memorandum.

asr-002475
02:13:09.740 --> 02:13:14.360
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So within 60 days, isasabit nila yan doon sa COA for

asr-002476
02:13:14.820 --> 02:13:17.960
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: for the publication together with the annual audit report.

asr-002477
02:13:18.120 --> 02:13:23.160
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So, June 30 ang deadline of the transmittal plus 60.

asr-002478
02:13:23.880 --> 02:13:26.380
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: So, talagang, tapos gagawin pa yan ng COA,

asr-002479
02:13:26.940 --> 02:13:29.060
COA Assistant Commissioner Nilda B. Plaras: iko-confirm pa yan, i-evaluate.

asr-002480
02:13:29.800 --> 02:13:32.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, talagang October 31?

asr-002481
02:13:33.920 --> 02:13:34.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sige, Chairman.

asr-002482
02:13:34.840 --> 02:13:36.760
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Ang ginagawa naman po namin, as soon as matapos,

asr-002483
02:13:36.760 --> 02:13:37.960
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: kasi hindi naman po sabay-sabay,

asr-002484
02:13:38.380 --> 02:13:43.680
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: as soon as matapos, pinapadala po namin agad sa inyo pong office.

asr-002485
02:13:43.680 --> 02:13:44.780
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, may mga hard copies po.

asr-002486
02:13:44.820 --> 02:13:45.880
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: So, pinapauna na po namin.

asr-002487
02:13:45.880 --> 02:13:48.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That would help a lot, especially during the budget process.

asr-002488
02:13:48.540 --> 02:13:49.540
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Pinapadala po namin agad.

asr-002489
02:13:49.640 --> 02:13:51.420
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: Basta po matapos, hindi lang po sabay-sabay.

asr-002490
02:13:52.040 --> 02:13:53.040
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: As it comes lang po.

asr-002491
02:13:54.920 --> 02:13:55.260
COA Chairperson Gamaliel A. Cordoba: We sent it to...

asr-002492
02:13:55.260 --> 02:13:58.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kinaaano kasi nila concerning availability raw sa public.

asr-002493
02:13:58.220 --> 02:14:02.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, if we can make it earlier nalang siguro, the earliest possible time.

asr-002494
02:14:02.740 --> 02:14:03.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung kaya lang naman po.

asr-002495
