Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: COA describes the citizen participatory audit as a mechanism

asr-002496
02:14:08.600 --> 02:14:12.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: that brings citizens and civil society organizations into the audit process.

asr-002497
02:14:12.940 --> 02:14:14.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nagamit na rin ito natin.

asr-002498
02:14:14.820 --> 02:14:21.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In previous audits, including in relation to the flood control master plan sa Kamanawa area.

asr-002499
02:14:21.840 --> 02:14:29.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For 2027, COA requested 40.7 million for CPA requirements under Tier 2,

asr-002500
02:14:29.140 --> 02:14:32.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but this was not included in the NEP.

asr-002501
02:14:33.100 --> 02:14:36.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, on follow-up, we have also received reports that in the past engagements,

asr-002502
